# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
# Master revision dictionary

REVISIONS = {
    ('abradsne.msg', '506'): 'You again? What do you want here? [His look hardens.] And have you got a reason to be holding a weapon?!',
    ('acanti.msg', '101'): 'You see a Mexican with long hair. He wears a canvas shirt, and a red bandana is tied around his head.',
    ('acanti.msg', '103'): 'I take it back. Looks like you can make it out here after all.',
    ('acanti.msg', '104'): 'I underestimated the captain. Looks like you can make it out here after all.',
    ('acanti.msg', '105'): "We're sailing home!",
    ('acanti.msg', '1202'): "You've talked to Cesareo already? He wants to put down roots in this bay. If you ask me, it's a piss-poor idea.",
    ('acanti.msg', '1218'): '(embraces you warmly) Fate itself sent you to us. Farewell, amiga.',
    ('acanti.msg', '1219'): 'Fate itself sent you to us. Farewell, amiga.',
    ('acanti.msg', '200'): 'Hey, amigo. You speak Spanish? Good. We need to talk.',
    ('acanti.msg', '202'): "You've talked to Cesareo already? He wants to put down roots in this bay. If you ask me, it's a piss-poor idea.",
    ('acanti.msg', '204'): "We're a long way from civilization. Out here you've got nobody to rely on but yourself. And what have we got? One boat and whatever pots we scavenged out of the ruins. Inland it's nothing but dead mountains. There is NOTHING here! Even the fish are far out to sea, because the coast is poisoned.",
    ('acanti.msg', '205'): 'So what do you suggest?',
    ('acanti.msg', '206'): "The captain brought us to the wrong place! Time to hand him the black spot and turn back for Mexico. And I'm not the only one who thinks so. Help us talk him around. Whatever he asks you to do - do the opposite. And if he still won't listen... then it comes to blood. Follow me?",
    ('acanti.msg', '207'): "All right. I'll keep that in mind.",
    ('acanti.msg', '208'): "Damn, life really put you through the wringer! Don't tell me this place is going to do the same to us. You speak Spanish, at least? Good. We need to talk.",
    ('acanti.msg', '210'): 'No man has set foot on this land since the day of the Apocalypse. We need to get out of here, and soon.',
    ('acanti.msg', '212'): 'The captain brought us to the wrong place! Time to hand him the black spot.',
    ('acanti.msg', '213'): "Your captain is dead. You're free to do as you please.",
    ('acanti.msg', '214'): "This is our chance! Time to get out of this cursed place. But there's one thing left to do - fix the water pump on the schooner. Without it we won't get far. She's moored at Fondeport.",
    ('acanti.msg', '215'): "All right. I'll see if I can fix it.",
    ('acanti.msg', '217'): "Cesareo has changed his mind. He's willing to sail now.",
    ('acanti.msg', '218'): '(shakes your hand firmly) Fate itself sent you to us. Farewell, amigo.',
    ('acanti.msg', '219'): 'Fate itself sent you to us. Farewell, amigo.',
    ('acanti.msg', '221'): 'Is that what this place does to people? Makes them into something like you? Bad business. We need to get out of here, and soon.',
    ('acanti.msg', '230'): "How do I change Cesareo's mind?",
    ('acanti.msg', '231'): "He has to see that nobody can survive here. Otherwise somebody's going to put scorpion venom in his food!",
    ('acanti.msg', '232'): "Hmm. That won't be easy.",
    ('acanti.msg', '233'): "Now the venom - that's not a bad idea.",
    ('acanti.msg', '235'): 'Better to smash the lighthouse mechanism outright, so it can never be lit.',
    ('acanti.msg', '236'): 'He asked me to look into the rumors of monsters on the shore.',
    ('acanti.msg', '238'): "There you go! That's a good reason to tell him this place isn't safe.",
    ('acanti.msg', '239'): 'He asked me to scout the area.',
    ('acanti.msg', '240'): "So lie to him! Tell him there's nothing out here worth living on.",
    ('acboss.msg', '104'): "I don't... feel so... good...",
    ('acboss.msg', '1260'): "It seems San Felipe bay has decided to have us after all. We have food and fresh water enough, we can sail out into deep water, and the monsters around us are no longer a threat. All of it thanks to you. Gracias, amiga. We're staying.",
    ('acboss.msg', '1262'): 'Now the bay is our home. Your help save us. We are happy. Many thanks, amiga.',
    ('acboss.msg', '1425'): 'The leeches had their lair in a grotto. I killed every last one of them.',
    ('acboss.msg', '203'): '(speaking Spanish) Very good. No need for a translator, then. I was beginning to think nobody in these parts spoke Spanish.',
    ('acboss.msg', '204'): 'Mexico is close enough that it still shows, even a century after the Great War. But you keep to yourselves out here?',
    ('acboss.msg', '205'): 'This is bad. I speak English very bad. (takes out a dictionary) But I have this book.',
    ('acboss.msg', '206'): "I don't think we'll manage much of a conversation. Still - what is this town?",
    ('acboss.msg', '207'): "We haven't settled on a name yet. There was a small town here once called San Felipe. Yes, we arrived not long ago. My name is Cesareo Villar Estrada, and I am captain of all these unfortunate people. Which is why I would like to know what to expect from you.",
    ('acboss.msg', '209'): "I'm just passing through. You've got nothing to worry about.",
    ('acboss.msg', '210'): 'I hope so. Forgive me, but we have our reasons for not trusting strangers.',
    ('acboss.msg', '212'): 'Eres un amigo o un enemigo? We want to know for sure.',
    ('acboss.msg', '213'): "Good. Make yourself useful and we won't run you off. That's fair enough.",
    ('acboss.msg', '214'): 'What can I do to change your opinion of me?',
    ('acboss.msg', '216'): "We're trying to make a life in a new place, and it hasn't been easy. Our fishermen need the lighthouse to put out to sea, but it doesn't work. We need the land around us surveyed - we don't even have a proper map. And Jan keeps complaining about monsters in the ship graveyard. I don't believe him, but it wouldn't hurt to check. Help us, since you're here.",
    ('acboss.msg', '217'): "All right. I'll see what I can do about all that.",
    ('acboss.msg', '218'): 'Lighthouse must be fixed. Need good map. Jan say he see monsters. I not believe Jan. You help us?',
    ('acboss.msg', '219'): "I'm here on behalf of the Brotherhood of Steel. They're your neighbors, and they'd like to make contact.",
    ('acboss.msg', '251'): '(speaking Spanish) So what is it you want?',
    ('acboss.msg', '260'): "It seems San Felipe bay has decided to have us after all. We have food and fresh water enough, we can sail out into deep water, and the monsters around us are no longer a threat. All of it thanks to you. Gracias, amigo. We're staying.",
    ('acboss.msg', '261'): "It's your right. You earned it. Good luck, Cesareo.",
    ('acboss.msg', '262'): 'Now the bay is our home. Your help save us. We are happy. Many thanks, amigo.',
    ('acboss.msg', '270'): 'I got the lighthouse working. Your fishermen can head out into deep water now.',
    ('acboss.msg', '271'): 'Excellent work! The water is cleaner out in the deep, and the fish are better for it. The coast was already fouled before the Great War. Your help is worth more than I can say. Thank you.',
    ('acboss.msg', '274'): "What's stopping you from getting the lighthouse running?",
    ('acboss.msg', '275'): "There are no spare parts out here. We've been through every ruin in San Felipe and found nothing worth having. It was a small town.",
    ('acboss.msg', '276'): 'Before I go hunting for parts, spare me a little more of your time.',
    ('acboss.msg', '277'): "I see. If I can't fix it myself, I'll look for parts in the nearby towns.",
    ('acboss.msg', '278'): 'The lighthouse is beyond repair. The mechanism has rotted away with age.',
    ('acboss.msg', '281'): "A thousand devils! We should have believed him. But you know, I think those things turned up only recently. Which means they're crawling out from somewhere while our backs are turned.",
    ('acboss.msg', '282'): 'Mil demonios! These monsters come in the night. We not know from where.',
    ('acboss.msg', '283'): "Then we need to find the giant leeches' lair and destroy it. Maybe Jan saw where they come out...",
    ('acboss.msg', '285'): 'Last I saw, he was by the burning barrel at the edge of the village.',
    ('acboss.msg', '286'): 'Before I go looking for him, one more question.',
    ('acboss.msg', '287'): "I'll go find him. So long.",
    ('acboss.msg', '290'): "The survey is done. Here's what's out there.",
    ('acboss.msg', '291'): "Thank you. So there's nobody out here at all. That suits us well. It's exactly why we sailed from Mexico - so that nobody would trouble us.",
    ('acboss.msg', '294'): 'What kind of map do you need?',
    ('acboss.msg', '295'): 'Anything! Most of all we need the lay of the land and where the fresh water is. Cover two sectors around San Felipe - that will do.',
    ('acboss.msg', '297'): "I'll head out now.",
    ('acboss.msg', '298'): "[lie] The survey is done. There's no fresh water to be found.",
    ('acboss.msg', '299'): 'I am sorry to hear it.',
    ('acboss.msg', '300'): 'Mind if I ask you a few questions?',
    ('acboss.msg', '302'): "Fair enough. We're not going to get far talking.",
    ('acboss.msg', '303'): "Ask away. It's good we speak the same language.",
    ('acboss.msg', '305'): 'Tell me about this village.',
    ('acboss.msg', '306'): "As I said, we came here by ship not long ago and haven't had time to settle in. There was a small port town here once, called San Felipe. By the time we arrived, nothing was left of it but empty ruins.",
    ('acboss.msg', '308'): "In the ship graveyard, near Jan's hut. It's a wonder that tub carried us this far at all.",
    ('acboss.msg', '309'): 'Why did you leave Mexico?',
    ('acboss.msg', '312'): "Oh, come on. Tell me - I'm curious.",
    ('acboss.msg', '313'): "Don't worry. There's nobody I could tell.",
    ('acboss.msg', '317'): "All right. Let's talk about something else.",
    ('acboss.msg', '318'): 'I think you can be trusted. The truth is we fled a civil war. Mexico is a restless place now - one faction takes over, then the next. We decided to look for somewhere quieter.',
    ('acboss.msg', '319'): "That's all?",
    ('acboss.msg', '320'): "We backed the wrong side, that's all. They sent troops to make an example of us. We fought them off, but it was plain they would grind us down in the end. To the new government we're traitors and enemies.",
    ('acboss.msg', '321'): 'Rough luck.',
    ('acboss.msg', '322'): "That's why we fled Mexico. Now you see why I didn't want to say? The government must never learn where we are.",
    ('acboss.msg', '324'): "You have powerful friends now. That's one thing you don't have to worry about.",
    ('acboss.msg', '326'): 'So what does that make you - war criminals?',
    ('acboss.msg', '330'): 'You know some of your people want to sail out of here?',
    ('acboss.msg', '331'): "I am doing what I can! Yes, this is barren country - but a gallows is waiting for us back home. It's time the rest of them admitted we have no choice. If we can't survive here, we're finished.",
    ('acboss.msg', '332'): "I won't argue. Just know that not everyone is happy with the way you're deciding things.",
    ('acboss.msg', '333'): "You'd be better off sailing somewhere else. You won't survive here.",
    ('acboss.msg', '334'): "If there's no living in this bay, we'll have to sail. But I need the survey done before I know that.",
    ('acboss.msg', '336'): "My survey shows there's little fresh water around here and no soil worth planting.",
    ('acboss.msg', '337'): 'Yes. But we can still live off the sea. Provided we get the lighthouse running.',
    ('acboss.msg', '341'): 'Yes. But we can still live off the sea. All the more so now that we have the lighthouse.',
    ('acboss.msg', '342'): "Bad news - the lighthouse is wrecked. There's no repairing it.",
    ('acboss.msg', '343'): "That's bad. Are there other settlements nearby, at least?",
    ('acboss.msg', '344'): "This is the back end of nowhere. On top of that you've got giant leeches and hostile savages for neighbors. And your own people are working up to a mutiny. You won't survive here.",
    ('acboss.msg', '345'): "A thousand devils! It seems this world has no place for us anywhere. But that's no reason to give up. We'll weigh anchor and find our own island paradise.",
    ('acboss.msg', '346'): "That's the spirit. I'll tell Hector what you've decided.",
    ('acboss.msg', '347'): "You'd be better off sailing somewhere else. There's no fresh water here and no soil worth planting. Giant leeches and hostile savages for neighbors. The lighthouse doesn't work. And your own people are working up to a mutiny. You won't survive here.",
    ('acboss.msg', '350'): "I'm here on behalf of the Brotherhood of Steel. That order is a power in these lands, and they want to know who you are.",
    ('acboss.msg', '351'): "A thousand devils! We were hoping this coast was corked up tight as a wine bottle. So we'll have to deal with neighbors after all?",
    ('acboss.msg', '352'): 'Less dealing with them than coming to terms - or bending the knee. That depends on you.',
    ('acboss.msg', '353'): 'Mil demonios! Son nuestros amigos o nuestros enemigos? We want to know for sure.',
    ('acboss.msg', '354'): "Enemies? No. They're the masters of this country. Not unless you make enemies of them.",
    ('acboss.msg', '355'): "So they're the masters of this country. Then let them prove they're worth reckoning with! We didn't flee Mexico just to kneel to another petty empire.",
    ('acboss.msg', '356'): "Solve your problems and you'll think differently. The Brotherhood is capable of a great deal more than that.",
    ('acboss.msg', '357'): "I speak for the Brotherhood of Steel, and I've already shown you what it can do. They have technology, weapons and reach. You'd do well to keep the order friendly.",
    ('acboss.msg', '358'): 'This order own this land? Then let order show its strength!',
    ('acboss.msg', '360'): "That's right. It seems you understand your position. I'll tell Paladin Latham you're ready to receive an envoy.",
    ('acboss.msg', '362'): 'Maldita sea! This order is strong.',
    ('acboss.msg', '400'): "What caught my eye in your survey was the fresh water. I'll send men out. Go with them and show them the place.",
    ('acboss.msg', '401'): 'I am interested in fresh water. You write there is a spring. You show?',
    ('acboss.msg', '402'): "All right. I'll take your men to the spring.",
    ('acboss.msg', '403'): "Give me a little time to get ready. I'll be back soon.",
    ('acboss.msg', '404'): "We found the fresh water. That's one thing off your mind.",
    ('acboss.msg', '405'): "And no trouble along the way? That's excellent news!",
    ('acboss.msg', '408'): "Bad news - the spring is held by a tribe of savages, and they're spoiling for a fight. You can't take them.",
    ('acboss.msg', '409'): "I didn't expect that! There are too few of us, and we've barely any weapons - we can't take that spring from savages.",
    ('acboss.msg', '411'): "I'm sorry. You'll have to make do with sea water.",
    ('acboss.msg', '412'): 'Let me go back out there. Maybe I can clear them out.',
    ('acboss.msg', '421'): 'Ask Jan. He knows more about those things than anyone.',
    ('acboss.msg', '422'): "I'll do that. Later.",
    ('acboss.msg', '423'): "I'll go see him now.",
    ('acboss.msg', '424'): "The leeches had their lair in a grotto. After a small explosion, nothing's coming out of it.",
    ('acboss.msg', '425'): 'The leeches had their lair in a grotto. I killed every last one of them.',
    ('acboss.msg', '426'): "Yo-ho-ho! Now we're in your debt, aren't we? Without you we'd have lost a lot of good people. Thank you.",
    ('acboss.msg', '427'): 'Yo-ho-ho! We be in your debt. Gracias!',
    ('acctzrun.msg', '102'): 'You see an agitated villager.',
    ('acctzrun.msg', '1215'): 'Tranquilo! (glances around) Sigueme, amiga. (waves for you to follow)',
    ('acctzrun.msg', '1255'): 'Ah! Gracias, amiga! Cuentale esto a nuestro capitan Cesareo.',
    ('acctzrun.msg', '215'): 'Tranquilo! (glances around) Sigueme, amigo. (waves for you to follow)',
    ('acctzrun.msg', '218'): '(as you reach the shore the villager points to his hut in the distance, then cries out in horror) Los monstruos!',
    ('acctzrun.msg', '247'): "No. We came in on a schooner a couple of years back. You'd do better asking our captain about that.",
    ('acctzrun.msg', '250'): "Like giant sea leeches, with disgusting tentacles in their mouths. I've never seen anything like them! They showed up after the last storm - washed in from somewhere deep, most likely. Who'd have thought there was anything out here to be afraid of?",
    ('acctzrun.msg', '251'): 'There really were monsters near your hut. I drove them off.',
    ('acctzrun.msg', '252'): "What did I tell you! Now Cesareo can't talk his way out of it! Everyone will know I was telling the truth - and they wouldn't believe me! But watch yourself. We still don't know how many of those things there are. Talk to Cesareo about it, he'll listen to you. I'm going to go check on my hut.",
    ('acctzrun.msg', '259'): 'I think they come out of that grotto over there at night.',
    ('acctzrun.msg', '261'): "I'll keep that in mind. Best not to go poking around in there just yet.",
    ('acctzrun.msg', '262'): '[Points at a large hill by the shore] La gruta.',
    ('acwtrpsn.msg', '101'): 'One of the San Felipe villagers. You need to escort him to the spring.',
    ('acwtrpsn.msg', '102'): 'Now we have fresh water! Go tell Cesareo.',
    ('acwtrpsn.msg', '111'): 'Damn it, savages have this place!',
    ('acwtrpsn.msg', '112'): "The savages hold the spring. We can't beat them.",
    ('acwtrpsn.msg', '113'): "It's the only drinking water for miles.",
    ('acwtrpsn.msg', '114'): "The savages won't give up the spring. What do we do now?",
    ('acwtrsvr.msg', '100'): 'A savage of Baja California.',
    ('acwtrsvr.msg', '101'): 'You see a warlike savage.',
    ('acwtrsvr.msg', '102'): 'This savage has no interest in talking to you.',
    ('afboat.msg', '201'): 'Cancel departure for now.',
    ('afcaptan.msg', '339'): "Any idea what's tearing up the nets?",
    ('afgirl.msg', '1243'): "As it happens, I was out on the platform and found this tag. It's got your family name on it.",
    ('aslampar.msg', '113'): 'The lighthouse mechanism is wrecked beyond repair!',
    ('asnasos.msg', '112'): 'You skillfully repair the water pump.',
    ('aswtrttm.msg', '102'): 'The totem vanishing without warning is bound to frighten the savages.',
    ('aswtrttm.msg', '103'): 'The totem vanishing would have frightened the savages - but there are no savages here any more.',
    ('aswtrttm.msg', '104'): 'The savages take the missing totems for the work of evil spirits and flee the valley!',
    ('bcboss.msg', '1216'): "Then remember you're an uninvited guest in our lands. If you won't help, at least stay out of our way.",
    ('bcboss.msg', '226'): "My village has just come through the hell of slavery. Now I'm looking for someone to protect it.",
    ('bcboss.msg', '268'): 'I hope your search for protectors for Villa goes just as well.',
    ('bcboss.msg', '269'): 'I hope your search for your missing people goes just as well. As it happens, our scouts reported a group of slaves from Villa seen on the road to Phoenix. Try there.',
    ('bcctznmt.msg', '1226'): "Nothing's too good for our hero. Here, have a plate.",
    ('bcfortun.msg', '1200'): "I knew you'd come here one day, farm girl from Villa. A sad tale, yours.",
    ('bcfortun.msg', '226'): 'Strange. The spirits say nothing of your future. Everything that mattered must already be behind you.',
    ('bcheadc.msg', '1218'): "Well now, an outsider in the pueblo. Who are you? What are you doing in another tribe's home?",
    ('bcheadc.msg', '1284'): "I'll make offerings to the Divine Brahmin, that it may guide and protect you on the road. Good luck, friend.",
    ('bcheadc.msg', '1291'): 'The Divine Brahmin itself must have had a hand in that. I see now I misjudged you. Not every outsider comes to conquer us or rob us. Thank you, friend from Villa.',
    ('bcmisbos.msg', '1227'): "Hm. Now I'm curious how you earned that much trust from Aaron himself. Maybe I should hear you out. But don't forget who commands this squad.",
    ('bcphill.msg', '1530'): "We can't sit outside Reno for days on end - nobody knows when or where they'll turn up next. Bartenders tell us somebody warns them over the radio when we're on the way, and they're gone every time. You don't look like one of us. You'll have an easier time catching them cold.",
    ('bcphill.msg', '1532'): "Fine work. You've done us a real service. People think little enough of us in Nevada as it is, and when that scum started running riot under our name... you don't forgive that. I hope they got everything that was coming to them.",
    ('bcphill.msg', '1533'): 'Uh, yeah. I did what needed doing.',
    ('bcphill.msg', '500'): "You don't hear that said often in Nevada...",
    ('bcphill.msg', '501'): 'Not interested, I think. Sorry - so long.',
    ('bcphill.msg', '502'): "Damn right. What happens inside the gang stays inside the gang. We keep to ourselves well enough to stay out of town squabbles. And somebody's been taking advantage of that.",
    ('bcphill.msg', '504'): "Normally the worst we leave behind is a good story about a drunken brawl. Lately there've been uglier things going around.",
    ('bcphill.msg', '506'): "Somebody's dragging our name through the dirt all over the state, making trouble in the towns and settlements out west. Sure, we raise hell now and then. But what those bastards are doing under our colors is plain robbery. And Nevada bikers aren't robbers.",
    ('bcphill.msg', '508'): 'Hm. Not a bad idea. Keep your ears open, then - I pay for good work.',
    ('bcphill.msg', '510'): "I'm not getting mixed up with people that dangerous. Count me out.",
    ('bcphill.msg', '511'): "Find those bastards and make them pay. How is up to you. And bring me back the jackets they've been scaring people with - nobody wears those but us. They came off dead bikers, besides, which matters to us just as much.",
    ('bcphill.msg', '513'): "Good. I'll wait to hear from you. If you like, I'll run you out to Reno and drop you at the edge of town so I don't get made. We can never catch the swine - somebody warns them over the radio when we're coming, and they're gone every time.",
    ('bcphill.msg', '516'): 'I had you figured for the robbers.',
    ('bcphill.msg', '517'): "When we have to, we'll gut any son of a bitch alive. But we don't do it for food and we don't do it for fun.",
    ('bcphill.msg', '521'): 'What, still dragging your feet?',
    ('bcphill.msg', '522'): "No, smart guy. It's done - I've got the jackets.",
    ('bcphill.msg', '523'): "Why can't you handle these bastards yourselves?",
    ('bcphill.msg', '526'): 'Almost... ah, forget it.',
    ('bcphill.msg', '527'): "For that? I'll drive you, no question. Heading out now?",
    ('bcphill.msg', '530'): "We can't sit outside Reno for days on end - nobody knows when or where they'll turn up next. Bartenders tell us somebody warns them over the radio when we're on the way, and they're gone every time. You don't look like one of us. You'll have an easier time catching them cold.",
    ('bcphill.msg', '532'): "Fine work. You've done us a real service. People think little enough of us in Nevada as it is, and when that scum started running riot under our name... you don't forgive that. I hope they got everything that was coming to them.",
    ('bcphill.msg', '533'): 'Uh, yeah. I did what needed doing.',
    ('bcphill.msg', '534'): "Good. Here's your pay. I figure we ought to see more of each other from here on - we like you.",
    ('bcphill.msg', '535'): "Some respect at last. That's more like it.",
    ('bcphill.msg', '536'): 'Hold up. People say a lot of good things about you. I know how hard it is, trying to stay honest and do right by people. I never managed it. But you... (takes out a revolver) Take it. Somebody like you should never be caught short around scum.',
    ('bcphill.msg', '537'): "Now that I'll thank you for!",
    ('bcphill.msg', '538'): 'Who do you figure is setting you up?',
    ('bcphill.msg', '539'): "Street punks out of New Reno, most likely. Wannabes with no instinct for self-preservation left. Then again, we're not short of enemies. Could be anyone.",
    ('bcphill.msg', '540'): 'Heard anything about the stagecoach robbery near Black Rock?',
    ('bcphill.msg', '541'): "Locals were talking about it. Doesn't interest me. Raiders, I'd bet.",
    ('bcphill.msg', '542'): 'Some people say it was the bikers.',
    ('bcphill.msg', '543'): "That so? Don't listen to spiteful talk. You wouldn't believe how many enemies and jealous little men have sprung up around this gang. But we're not bandits and we don't rob stagecoaches. That one's not ours.",
    ('bcranger.msg', '276'): 'See if you can stand up FOR YOURSELF first, FOOL!',
    ('ccboss.msg', '1202'): "What's going on? Ah, gringa, we're celebrating our saints' day. You've walked into a feast! Help yourself, make yourself at home. Everyone is welcome here... everyone who doesn't get in our way.",
    ('ccboss.msg', '1242'): "Here's how it is, gringa. Leave, and don't ever come back.",
    ('ccboss.msg', '1251'): 'Fifteen years I kept these people safe. And this is how they repay me! Now that El Diablo is gone, any one of them is free to point a finger. Do you have any idea what those sacrifices cost me? How I suffered through the first years? But I did the very thing they made me elder to do - I saved them. And now you tell me it was wrong? To hell with your opinion, cursed gringa!',
    ('ccninb.msg', '1226'): "(falls to her knees and sobs) But El Diablo... *sniff-sniff* You don't understand, gringa. They raised me for this my whole life. I always knew this day would come.",
    ('ccnino.msg', '1238'): "You're a gringa, you don't understand! If she takes the crown I won't be allowed near her again. And I... I love her...",
    ('ccpapa.msg', '1301'): "Every few months we gave him a sacrifice, one we'd raised for the purpose. And so that nobody would lose heart, Hilario turned it into a ceremony and started preaching about divine cleansing. That's how we lived, hand in hand with a real devil. Until you turned up, gringa.",
    ('cfrancis.msg', '20550'): "I'm the sheriff around here, and I haven't got time for you.",
    ('cfrancis.msg', '20600'): "I already told you I'm busy. Still true.",
    ('cmbatai2.msg', '32021'): 'Aaaargh!',
    ('containr.msg', '210'): ' skillfully sets a trap on the container.',
    ('containr.msg', '211'): ' -- cannot set a trap on the container.',
    ('dcbarshf.msg', '105'): "We finish Bustos, and that's the end of it.",
    ('dcbarshf.msg', '106'): "It all worked out very neatly. We'll put it down to a highwayman attack.",
    ('dcctzne.msg', '280'): 'Fue muy dificil cruzar el desierto. Pero lo hicimos porque no teniamos otra opcion. Primero llegamos a la ciudad de Two-Sun, y de ahi nos echaron. Luego nos quedamos en Casa Grande.',
    ('dcctzne.msg', '372'): 'He never came back to Two-Sun. What do you know about it?',
    ('dcctzne.msg', '373'): "You didn't hear this from me, amigo, but you'll find your answer in the local cemetery. And don't ask me about it again.",
    ('dcmer.msg', '1448'): 'Shut your mouth and listen. I am the MAYOR OF THIS TOWN. I answer for it. And I will let NO ONE drag its name through the dirt. Who are you to judge me? An outsider passing through, nothing more. So be on your way!',
    ('dcmer.msg', '1548'): "Hey, where's my reward? I didn't haul rotting flesh across those baking highways for my health.",
    ('dcmerdch.msg', '107'): 'Papa is gone and Sullivan has taken the town. And me along with it. How did it come to this?!',
    ('dcmerdch.msg', '351'): "Between us, he's already in the ground. Go check the cemetery if you don't believe me.",
    ('dcmerdch.msg', '352'): "Damn. That's not a pleasant errand...",
    ('dcmerstp.msg', '105'): 'Whoa, whoa! I want no part of this!',
    ('dcmerstp.msg', '106'): "Looks like it's time I got out of this town. Damn. And it all started so well...",
    ('dcmerstp.msg', '205'): 'Okay.',
    ('dcmerstp.msg', '264'): 'Anybody home?',
    ('dcmerstp.msg', '271'): "That's right. They had him in the bathtub not an hour ago. But the little swine is tough - he won't crack easy.",
    ('dcwtratk.msg', '217'): 'Nooo! [try to hug them and calm them down]',
    ('dcwtrbos.msg', '104'): "I'll run this town my own way. Relax, take a bath. I've told the trader to give you a discount.",
    ('dcwtrbos.msg', '1231'): 'No problem. I saw nothing and I heard nothing.',
    ('dcwtrbos.msg', '253'): "I'm tracking a slave convoy. It was headed for Two-Sun.",
    ('dcwtrbos.msg', '254'): "Then go to Two-Sun. It's further south down the highway. Caravans don't stop here for long.",
    ('dcwtrbos.msg', '320'): "Try asking the mayor. There's no more work at my station.",
    ('dcwtrbos.msg', '322'): 'All right. Can I take a little more of your time?',
    ('dcwtrbos.msg', '330'): "About the pump. What's stopping you from fixing the filter?",
    ('dcwtrbos.msg', '331'): "The tinkers skin you three times over for any job. They know water is the most valuable thing there is. But we can't hand them everything we have. And nobody else can do that kind of work - they're the only ones with the machines, the knowledge and the hands for it.",
    ('dcwtrbos.msg', '333'): "The filter's fine. Dirt and sand had chewed up a few parts, but I got them working again.",
    ('dcwtrbos.msg', '334'): "Work like that is worth paying for. Take it, here's ",
    ('dcwtrbos.msg', '338'): "For any more than that I wouldn't have offered the job at all.",
    ('dcwtrbos.msg', '341'): 'That barely covers what the extra parts cost me.',
    ('dcwtrbos.msg', '350'): "I know you and Bustos don't see eye to eye. Want to talk about it?",
    ('dcwtrbos.msg', '352'): "Well, strictly speaking, you're right.",
    ('dcwtrbos.msg', '353'): "You've got a quarrel with Bustos. So do the highwaymen. Maybe we join forces?",
    ('dcwtrbos.msg', '355'): 'Nothing. Just talking nonsense. Pay no attention.',
    ('dcwtrbos.msg', '356'): "The highwaymen want the mayor gone. They'll never come to terms with him. With you, they might.",
    ('dcwtrbos.msg', '357'): "Bustos has worn my patience through. He brought order here once, I'll grant him that. But now he drinks his days away at the bottom of a bottle while I break my back on this cursed water plant!",
    ('dcwtrbos.msg', '358'): "Sounds like it's time he retired.",
    ('dcwtrbos.msg', '359'): "I've made up my mind! I'll gather my men and take this town for myself! To the town hall...",
    ('dcwtrbos.msg', '360'): 'Whoa - that fast?',
    ('dcwtrbos.msg', '361'): "I don't imagine it's easy for him either. Cool off for now.",
    ('dcwtrgrd.msg', '131'): 'We need a new boss. Otherwise this whole place comes apart.',
    ('dcwtrgrd.msg', '133'): 'What the hell do we do now?',
    ('dcwtrgrd.msg', '143'): 'Somebody should have thrown out that gutless mayor years ago.',
    ('dcwtrgrd.msg', '150'): 'Sooner we finish, sooner we go home.',
    ('ecbandit.msg', '203'): 'Everything valuable. On the ground. Now.',
    ('ecbandit.msg', '207'): "No panic, now. It'll all be over in a minute.",
    ('ecbandit.msg', '208'): "Let's see what we've got here.",
    ('ecbandit.msg', '210'): "Don't make this hard on yourself.",
    ('ecbandit.msg', '211'): 'Hand it over.',
    ('ecbandit.msg', '214'): "I promise I'll make it quick.",
    ('ecbandit.msg', '215'): 'Straight up to heaven with you.',
    ('ecdogmet.msg', '103'): 'The Dog barks and barks. He wants to come with you.',
    ('ecdogmet.msg', '105'): 'Maybe you come with me when I got more room.',
    ('ecdogmet.msg', '106'): 'Easy, boy. Stay.',
    ('ecdogmet.msg', '107'): "Come on, Dog. Let's go bite somebody.",
    ('ecdogmet.msg', '108'): "Don't worry, boy. I'll come back for you when there's room in the party.",
    ('ecdogmet.msg', '110'): 'The Dog wolfs down the iguana-on-a-stick and looks up at you expectantly.',
    ('ecdogmet.msg', '112'): 'Maybe you come with me when I got more room.',
    ('ecdogmet.msg', '113'): 'Easy, boy. Stay.',
    ('ecdogmet.msg', '114'): "Come on, Dog. Let's go bite somebody.",
    ('ecdogmet.msg', '115'): "Don't worry, boy. I'll come back for you when there's room in the party.",
    ('ecdogmet.msg', '119'): 'Maybe you come with me when I got more room.',
    ('ecdogmet.msg', '120'): "Stay, boy. Don't follow.",
    ('ecdogmet.msg', '122'): "Come on, Dog. Let's go bite somebody.",
    ('ecdogmet.msg', '123'): "I'll come back for you when I've got room.",
    ('ecdogmet.msg', '124'): 'Stay close to me. All right?',
    ('ecdogmet.msg', '125'): 'Keep your distance.',
    ('ecdogmet.msg', '126'): 'Stay well back. Watch my back.',
    ('ecdogmet.msg', '128'): "All right, let's move.",
    ('ecdogmet.msg', '129'): 'The Dog yelps sharply, then drops into a low growl.',
    ('ecdogmet.msg', '130'): 'Stay close to me. All right?',
    ('ecdogmet.msg', '131'): 'Keep your distance.',
    ('ecdogmet.msg', '132'): 'Stay well back. Watch my back.',
    ('ecdogmet.msg', '134'): 'Thanks, Dog. You bite bad man good.',
    ('ecdogmet.msg', '137'): 'Hey, friend, you mess with my dog.',
    ('ecdogmet.msg', '139'): 'Dog! Heel!',
    ('encmtntc.msg', '1243'): "I've joined the Brotherhood of Steel myself, not long ago. Well met, brother.",
    ('encmtntc.msg', '300'): "Reactor's down. Time to clear out.",
    ('encmtntc.msg', '301'): "As an engineer it hurts me to see good machinery wrecked. But there was no other way. The mutants won't get that platform running again, and out in the middle of the desert they're no danger to anyone.",
    ('encmtntc.msg', '303'): 'Ba-boom! Me do it all!',
    ('encmtntc.msg', '304'): "Reactor's already dead. Time to clear out.",
    ('encmtntc.msg', '311'): 'Supermutts - all gone! Me go ba-boom on their heads!',
    ('encmtntc.msg', '312'): "Now that's something! Ah, we could have used soldiers like you in the Great War against the super mutants.",
    ('encmtntc.msg', '314'): 'No need for that. The super mutants are dead and the way is clear.',
    ('encmtntc.msg', '320'): 'The main thing now is to not draw attention. We need to put enough distance between us and the platform that nobody spots us.',
    ('encmtntc.msg', '323'): 'Okay.',
    ('encmtntc.msg', '324'): "If I make it through, I'll tell the order about you. High time I remembered everything they taught me back at the base. Maybe we'll meet again in Puerto Penasco, if the road takes you that way.",
    ('encmtntc.msg', '326'): 'Bye now!',
    ('encslvc.msg', '1207'): "If you really are a Follower of the Fire, you ought to know this: when you're not let in on the important business, it's because you haven't earned it.",
    ('fcadmin.msg', '284'): "My people at Villa are afraid they'll be taken to the mines again.",
    ('fcadmin.msg', '285'): 'Stupid yokels! All we want is for the mine to WORK.',
    ('fcadmin.msg', '286'): "So if I fix your labor problem, you'll leave Villa alone? What exactly needs doing?",
    ('fcadmin.msg', '287'): "Stupid yokels! All we want is for the mine to WORK. And it's working better now than it ever has.",
    ('fcadmin.msg', '288'): "So you don't need workers from Villa any more? That's good news. I'll tell the council of elders.",
    ('fcbartlk.msg', '1214'): "Hey there, friend. You're the one who finished Faber, aren't you? Nice work. Going to stand me a drink?",
    ('fcbartlk.msg', '213'): "Ugh, what a face on you! Don't even think about coming near me until you buy me a drink.",
    ('fcbartlk.msg', '214'): "Hey there, pal. You're the one who finished Faber, aren't you? Nice work. Going to stand me a drink?",
    ('fcbartlk.msg', '249'): "You really think so? I don't want to lose him. Maybe I'll try settling down here after all.",
    ('fcbartlk.msg', '250'): "Don't second-guess yourself. Carl turned criminal for your sake. Don't turn your back on him now.",
    ('fcbartlk.msg', '262'): "(takes a hard pull from the bottle) Ah, fine. You may be short on brains, but I'll tell you my story.",
    ('fcbartlk.msg', '266'): '[Put a hand on her shoulder and nod]',
    ('fcbartlk.msg', '267'): 'Okay!',
    ('fcbartlk.msg', '268'): "I don't suppose you follow much of what I say. But you helped me make up my mind. Thank you.",
    ('fcboss.msg', '1372'): "I named a price for the problem being dealt with. All you brought me was information. It isn't worth more than that.",
    ('fcboss.msg', '370'): "It was a ranger, working alone. He's dug into the museum basement.",
    ('fcboss.msg', '371'): "A ranger? A common criminal who fancies himself a hero. I'll send a squad. We'll smoke the son of a bitch out. And here's 50 caps for the information.",
    ('fcboss.msg', '372'): "I named a price for the problem being dealt with. All you brought me was information. It isn't worth more than that.",
    ('fcboss.msg', '380'): "Here's the thing. The elders are afraid of being enslaved all over again.",
    ('fcboss.msg', '381'): "A healthy fear of authority is no bad thing. But my mine doesn't need that many hands any more - it's running at full capacity. I doubt I'll be sending another convoy.",
    ('fcboss.msg', '382'): "That's reassuring. I'll pass your words along to them.",
    ('fcboss.msg', '383'): "If the mine were running at full capacity I'd never have had to resort to slavery. Until I get it running properly, I'll keep taking hands wherever I can find them.",
    ('fcboss.msg', '385'): "What's wrong with this mine, then?",
    ('fcctzna.msg', '1201'): "That's hardly a gracious way to greet a guest.",
    ('fcfarmb.msg', '1205'): "You're as much a hypocrite as the rest of the newcomers. You came to these lands, slaughtered our people and took what was ours. We're only taking it back.",
    ('fckidpap.msg', '227'): "I'm working on it. Give me a little time.",
    ('fckidpap.msg', '228'): "You're welcome. But I need to be going.",
    ('fcoxdoc.msg', '102'): 'The doctor is thinking hard about something. Medical business, probably.',
    ('fcoxdoc.msg', '112'): ". That's a strange name. What does it mean?",
    ('fcoxdoc.msg', '113'): "It isn't all that white. Looks more like a dirty rag.",
    ('fcoxdoc.msg', '115'): 'Can you get the radiation and the poison out of me?',
    ('fcoxdoc.msg', '116'): "Show me what you've got.",
    ('fcoxdoc.msg', '118'): "I don't have that many caps. I'd better go.",
    ('fcoxdoc.msg', '121'): 'So where are you from?',
    ('fcoxdoc.msg', '122'): '<Listen, could you operate on me somehow - make me stronger, or smarter?^Listen, could you operate on me somehow - make me stronger, or smarter?>',
    ('fcoxdoc.msg', '220'): 'Another customer.',
    ('fcoxdoc.msg', '221'): '<You blind? White coat. That makes me the doctor. Cox, since you asked.^You blind? White coat. That makes me the doctor. Cox, since you asked.>',
    ('fcoxdoc.msg', '222'): '<None of your business. Say what you came for or clear off.^None of your business. Say what you came for or clear off.>',
    ('fcoxdoc.msg', '223'): "<We've got a comedian. If you're not here for help, shut the door on your way out.^We've got a comedian. If you're not here for help, shut the door on your way out.>",
    ('fcoxdoc.msg', '224'): "I could take off an arm or a leg. Joking - relax, mostly it's just fingers. Listen, I treat the whole carcass or nothing: breaks, scrapes, bad health, all of it together. Costs you a measly 150 caps.",
    ('fcoxdoc.msg', '225'): "No problem. That'll be 50 caps.",
    ('fcoxdoc.msg', '226'): "Look - all that matters is whether you've got the caps.",
    ('fcoxdoc.msg', '227'): "<Don't play me for a fool, there's nothing wrong with you. Clear off.^Don't play me for a fool, there's nothing wrong with you. Clear off.>",
    ('fcoxdoc.msg', '228'): "Don't distract me. What do you want?",
    ('fcoxdoc.msg', '229'): "We'll have this sorted in a minute. Just don't twitch and don't scream.",
    ('fcoxdoc.msg', '230'): 'You scream like a girl. Ha-ha-ha.',
    ('fcoxdoc.msg', '231'): 'You scream like a boy. Ha-ha-ha.',
    ('fcoxdoc.msg', '232'): "Hold still, we're going to flush your system out [you may have misheard, but he said something about an enema].",
    ('fcoxdoc.msg', '233'): "You haven't got any of that muck in you. Stop inventing things.",
    ('fcoxdoc.msg', '234'): "I came here from Clineck, after they leveled it. Big fight there between the military and the raiders - nothing left of the town but rubble. I wandered the irradiated wastes a while, then settled here, and I haven't regretted it yet. Truth is I'd rather not think about it. It was a long time ago.",
    ('fcoxdoc.msg', '235'): "Can't do that sort of thing. Takes special equipment and knowledge both. I hear the Brotherhood of Steel worked in that line, but they're a long way from here. Never seen them in this region.",
    ('fcpost.msg', '260'): 'Can I leave my things with you?',
    ('fcpost.msg', '261'): 'Of course. We have storage lockers - combination lock, watched around the clock. Each locker costs ',
    ('fcpost.msg', '263'): "That's more than I can afford.",
    ('fcpost.msg', '264'): "Good. I'll take a locker.",
    ('fcpost.msg', '265'): 'Very good. You can use it any time.',
    ('fcpost.msg', '267'): 'I need another locker.',
    ('fcranger.msg', '1343'): "There aren't many of my people left. I doubt you've ever heard of us.",
    ('fcranger.msg', '239'): "Your traps might work on children. On anyone who knows what they're doing, I doubt it.",
    ('fcranger.msg', '253'): 'Chinga tu madre! When did you last see a colonist speak Spanish?',
    ('fcranger.msg', '302'): 'Bye now.',
    ('fcranger.msg', '324'): "No. But I'm not the one who dragged you here.",
    ('fcranger.msg', '424'): 'Thanks for the answer.',
    ('fcslvbld.msg', '1208'): "Hey, you don't look like one of the overseers. Caravan hand, are you?",
    ('fctom.msg', '1202'): "Ah, so you're another one chasing a uranium vein? Forget it. This town stopped being the place on those posters a long time ago. You want to earn here, you'll work yourself into the ground.",
    ('fsminelc.msg', '113'): 'The victim is too far from the bare wire.',
    ('gcbarmen.msg', '375'): 'If I wind up there, I could talk to someone about liquor supplies.',
    ('gcboss.msg', '1356'): 'I could do with some makeup before a job like this. Back soon.',
    ('gcctza.msg', '217'): 'To sweeten up a stranger, open your backpack and hand them something to eat.',
    ('gcgate.msg', '344'): "Follow the highway due east. It'll take a few days. But in your place I'd cut through the wastes. Mark my words - better to meet a wild animal than a man on the open road.",
    ('gcgate.msg', '384'): "I've got a spare rifle that still works. We'll strip it for parts.",
    ('gcmotlc.msg', '1220'): "Nobody around here knows you, you lousy little shrew. You don't scare us.",
    ('gcom6rea.msg', '1100'): 'Thermal performance: 6000 MW\r\n                                        Electrical performance: 1900 MW\r\n                                    Steam production: 10200t/hour\r\n                                    Temperature: 318 deg C',
    ('gcom6rea.msg', '1150'): 'Thermal performance: 6000 MW\r\n                                        Electrical performance: 1900 MW\r\n                                    Steam production: 10200t/hour\r\n                                    Temperature: 1200 deg C... 1400 deg C... 1600 deg C',
    ('gcpit.msg', '1200'): 'Oh! Greetings, companera! First time in town?',
    ('gcpit.msg', '245'): "Hold on, we're not finished yet.",
    ('gcpit.msg', '331'): "I'll keep it in mind, in case something needs fixing.",
    ('gcpit.msg', '356'): "That'll run you ",
    ('guyvik.msg', '101'): "He's probably the dog's owner.",
    ('guyvik.msg', '103'): "You gain 500 experience points for gaining man's best friend.",
    ('guyvik.msg', '200'): 'Hello. You need something?',
    ('guyvik.msg', '201'): "That's a fine dog you've got. Will you sell him?",
    ('guyvik.msg', '202'): "What's that mangy dog doing next to you?",
    ('guyvik.msg', '203'): 'Get lost, before I set him on you.',
    ('guyvik.msg', '204'): "That dog and I have walked most of Nevada together. He's pulled me out of trouble more than once. I'm too old to roam the way I used to, but he still wants the road. Twenty-five hundred and he's yours. You won't regret it.",
    ('guyvik.msg', '205'): "That's steep. Take 500 off?",
    ('guyvik.msg', '206'): "Maybe I did ask too much. Two thousand and we've got a deal.",
    ('guyvik.msg', '207'): "That won't do. I need the whole amount.",
    ('guyvik.msg', '209'): "Here you go. That's all of it.",
    ('guyvik.msg', '210'): 'By the way - what are you and your dog called?',
    ('guyvik.msg', '211'): "I'm Vic. The dog's Blood, though I've never called him anything but dog. Right. I'll go find somewhere to sit, I'm tired of standing around here. So long, and good luck out there [he whistles to the dog one last time and walks away].",
    ('guyvik.msg', '212'): "That's a lot of money. I'll need to save up.",
    ('guyvik.msg', '213'): "Well then. Where's my money?",
    ('guyvik.msg', '214'): "That's steep. Take 1000 off?",
    ('guyvik.msg', '215'): "Maybe I did ask too much. Fifteen hundred and we've got a deal.",
    ('hcboss.msg', '1203'): 'What are you babbling about? Seize the spy!',
    ('hcpost.msg', '1237'): "A gringa from the north, one of us? That's a joke. Believe me, there's nothing for you here.",
    ('hcprisnr.msg', '1340'): "Must be something, having a home and a family of your own. Let's go, companera. I'll watch your back.",
    ('hcprisnr.msg', '267'): "I've never been here before. Isn't this your village?",
    ('icapoc.msg', '1518'): "You're not about to leave me behind, are you, sunshine?",
    ('icgate.msg', '1200'): "What's this? Another normie? And she walked in on her own? Ho-ho-ho, this is our lucky day!",
    ('iclabrnt.msg', '131'): "Now you'll know every bit of the pain we called down. My sympathies.",
    ('iclabrnt.msg', '132'): 'Shall I irradiate a little coffee for you?',
    ('iclabrnt.msg', '133'): 'Those big green-skinned idiots giving you trouble?',
    ('iclabrnt.msg', '135'): 'Do as Levi says. He stood close to the Creator himself!',
    ('icmaster.msg', '1112'): 'Receive the sinful soul of your servant...',
    ('icmaster.msg', '1208'): "Courteous, with a six-barreled minigun in my face? You're not very gracious yourself, for a priest.",
    ('icmaster.msg', '1231'): "There's no way out for you. Garrett, explain that to our guest...",
    ('icmaster.msg', '1246'): "Well, I understand. You're alone, as we all are. But you have friends now. You have my word - you'll be happy with us.",
    ('icmaster.msg', '1334'): "How very discourteous. Garrett, show our guest that she's no longer welcome...",
    ('icpaladn.msg', '1204'): "So you're nothing but a scavenger? Bah. Looks like I used up all my luck last year.",
    ('icpaladn.msg', '1498'): "You're a redneck out of your own damn mind! You should have died in the womb!",
    ('jcsamec.msg', '1247'): "I don't trust outsiders. And that's what you are.",
    ('jcsuka.msg', '1104'): "Foolish outsider - that poison doesn't work on Jackals!",
    ('jcsuka.msg', '1253'): "The rangers fed us, just as they promised. We've no taste for plant food, but no belly in this pack goes empty now. We all owe you - messenger of the Holy Jackal.",
    ('jstotem.msg', '133'): 'This is part of their culture. Why do that to them?',
    ('jstotem.msg', '136'): "Ha! I'd love to see the savages' faces when they find this.",
    ('lcclbsuz.msg', '161'): "(beams at you and waves it off) Oh! Don't be silly! Worse things have happened in here! The things this old girl has lived through! Don't you worry yourself. It's all right!",
    ('leonkill.msg', '101'): 'You see Leon, quietly taking everything in.',
    ('leonkill.msg', '102'): 'You see Leon. He looks like he wants to shoot somebody.',
    ('leonkill.msg', '103'): "You see Leon. He looks like he couldn't care less about anything.",
    ('leonkill.msg', '167'): "Wait, don't rush me.",
    ('leonkill.msg', '200'): "Hey there, drifter. Name's Leon. The lights of Vegas get you too?",
    ('leonkill.msg', '202'): "You come in off the desert or something? Vegas is a dream. Vegas is money and girls and easy living. Shame I blew every bit of it [he sighs]. Went through my savings first, then sold my favorite rifle to Paul Tibbet, the trader here. Without that rifle I can't even take to the road.",
    ('leonkill.msg', '203'): 'If I buy your rifle back, will you come with me?',
    ('leonkill.msg', '204'): "Sure. I'm done gambling anyway - the casinos here are all card sharps and damned cheats. Tibbet's shop is close by. Fair warning, though: he's a tight-fisted old goat.",
    ('leonkill.msg', '205'): "Wait here. I'll go see what I can do.",
    ('leonkill.msg', '300'): "Ah, you're back. Did you get my rifle?",
    ('leonkill.msg', '301'): 'Not yet. Be patient.',
    ('leonkill.msg', '302'): "Took some doing, but I got it. Here's your rifle. Let's go - no reason to hang around here.",
    ('leonkill.msg', '303'): "Now that's good news. Let's go shoot something. Aim for the head or the groin, it's more dependable [he laughs loudly].",
    ('leonkill.msg', '5008'): 'I love that rifle, but I can handle most others, and I can do some damage with a knife. The rest I\'ve no use for. Anyway, like an old friend of mine used to say - Mathilda, her name was: "One shot, one corpse."',
    ('leonkill.msg', '508'): 'What weapons do you use?',
    ('leonkill.msg', '510'): 'Do you know how to make stimpaks?',
    ('leonkill.msg', '512'): 'Remind me what a stimpak takes?',
    ('leonkill.msg', '513'): "Thanks. You're a help.",
    ('leonkill.msg', '515'): 'I make stimpaks out of moonshine and a mutfruit. And you need a syringe.',
    ('leonkill.msg', '516'): "I'll need one bottle of moonshine, one mutfruit and a syringe.",
    ('leonkill.msg', '517'): 'Getting to work... [You watch Leon put a stimpak together.]',
    ('leonkill.msg', '552'): "A couple of stimpaks wouldn't hurt.",
    ('leonkill.msg', '560'): "I'll try to keep up.",
    ('leonkill.msg', '561'): "I'll keep a middle distance.",
    ('leonkill.msg', '562'): "I'll hang well back.",
    ('leonkill.msg', '563'): 'I need you to stay close to me.',
    ('leonkill.msg', '564'): "Don't get too far from me.",
    ('mcboss.msg', '1267'): "I'll be honest, I hadn't heard any of that. Now I definitely don't want to help Bustos.",
    ('mcboss.msg', '225'): 'Do the job first. Then you get them back.',
    ('mcboss.msg', '227'): '(Signals to his men, and they hand back what was taken from you when you first met.)',
    ('mcboss.msg', '229'): "I'm no use to you dead on the road. I need my things.",
    ('mcmtlnew.msg', '250'): "Aaron and his cathedral have fallen. You hadn't heard?",
    ('mcmtlnew.msg', '251'): 'How dare you say such a thing?! Aaron is alive, of course, and his church has never been stronger! Shut your vile mouth before I lose my temper.',
    ('mcrdrhak.msg', '1239'): "A favor for a favor, that's all. Just remember who your real amiga is around here.",
    ('mcrio.msg', '1205'): "(his lip curling on one side) Look who's come to see us. Ben's new favorite bitch!",
    ('mcrio.msg', '1225'): 'Yes. Exactly that. You should have led with it. Hm. Maybe we can work together after all.',
    ('misc.msg', '50'): 'Fallout needs the disc in the drive to run!',
    ('ncapcbos.msg', '1455'): "I've been there. The place really is cursed. And anything worth taking was hauled off long ago.",
    ('ncapcbos.msg', '228'): "You've really got nothing to pay with? You look like a person of some means.",
    ('ncapcbos.msg', '229'): 'Forgive me, I never meant to cheat you...',
    ('ncapcbos.msg', '246'): "Actually, I don't need treatment.",
    ('nchimadr.msg', '1251'): "Don't go against the rules, dear viajera. Those prohibitions at the main gate are written in blood.",
    ('ncmer.msg', '236'): "What do we do now? Who's going to protect us? Who's going to tell us what to do?",
    ('ncmer.msg', '238'): "The Followers of the Apocalypse aren't fighters, and there are barely any of them. It's hopeless... It's all over... all over...",
    ('ncsherif.msg', '1223'): "Get this straight, outsider. I don't like people stirring up panic and spreading rumors in my town. Don't make things worse for yourself. Simple as that.",
    ('ncsherif.msg', '1244'): "My apologies, sheriff. I don't know the local rules very well.",
    ('ncsherif.msg', '1317'): "All in all, nicely done, warrior. You'd do well in our ranks.",
    ('ncstragn.msg', '119'): "Striker's about to close a deal on a weapons shipment. I'll tell you everything I know, but there's a condition - I want over to Thompson's side, and soon.",
    ('ncstragn.msg', '120'): "Thompson's people have no use for turncoats. Once Striker's been dealt with they won't cut you any slack - don't kid yourself. Get out of here, and go a long way.",
    ('ncstragn.msg', '121'): "Feeling the heat? You should be. Striker's whole gang is about to go under, and you'll be standing in the middle of it if you don't move fast. I'll pass your request to Thompson.",
    ('ncstragn.msg', '122'): "So that's how it is - shopping yourself around for a better price? There's a name for that. Political prostitution. Bah! But fine - maybe... *maybe* Thompson will have you.",
    ('ncstragn.msg', '123'): "Really? Then I'm finished! You're saying I should run... Well. I've got no choice. Lie low in one of those little villages, take up farming, or hunting. Probably ought to start walking right now.",
    ('ncstragn.msg', '124'): "They'll take me? Really? That's great! I've wanted to go over to him for ages, honestly! But it isn't that simple, you understand?",
    ('ncstragn.msg', '125'): "No, no! It's just that I used to, er, see things differently. Then I heard what Thompson stands for and, er, my eyes opened! Honestly! I'll work hard, I'll be useful - just give me a chance!",
    ('ncstragn.msg', '126'): "Yes, yes. Now, about Striker's deal.",
    ('ncstragn.msg', '129'): "Er, that's the one thing I couldn't get... But I know the data sits on a terminal in the generator room. There's a back way in, but the doors are locked.",
    ('p_party_orders.msg', '0'): '** Player autoloot disabled **',
    ('p_party_orders.msg', '1'): '** Player autoloot enabled **',
    ('p_party_orders.msg', '1201'): 'Everyone patch yourselves up, quick.',
    ('p_party_orders.msg', '1400'): 'Pick up the loot, ',
    ('p_party_orders.msg', '1410'): "That's enough. Get back, ",
    ('p_party_orders.msg', '1415'): "I can't carry any more.",
    ('p_party_orders.msg', '1421'): "I'm done.",
    ('p_party_orders.msg', '1423'): "That's the lot.",
    ('p_party_orders.msg', '1499'): 'Everyone is overloaded. Nobody can carry any more.',
    ('p_party_orders.msg', '1600'): 'Fall back, ',
    ('p_party_orders.msg', '2002'): 'Party members: burst fire on.',
    ('p_party_orders.msg', '2003'): 'Party members: burst fire off.',
    ('pcatmwrk.msg', '1102'): "Well, well. If it isn't our chief troublemaker. Clear off while your legs still work!",
    ('pcbaika.msg', '113'): "You won't find him here. He lost his head and went straight into the middle of Hawthorne.",
    ('pcbaika.msg', '124'): "Oh, really? Jay hasn't been in touch with us about it. We've been waiting on that news a good while, and the rednecks around here are starting to wear on us. We'll move on the base as soon as everyone's ready.",
    ('pcbdbkr.msg', '1240'): "You're a fool for picking a fight with a champion. Want me to show you a few moves?",
    ('pcbdctz.msg', '1100'): 'You see a woman of the slums.',
    ('pcbdctz.msg', '1101'): 'You see a woman of the slums. A pitiful sight.',
    ('pcbdctz.msg', '1102'): 'You see a woman of the slums. She is digging in her ear.',
    ('pcbdctz.msg', '1104'): 'You see a woman of the slums. She is fussing fondly over the only rags she owns.',
    ('pcbdctz.msg', '1105'): 'You see a local woman. The bald patches on her scalp say a good deal about conditions in the slums.',
    ('pcbdded.msg', '241'): "Ah, right. This is the common house, and I'm Bob - scavenger and odd-job man. Follow? You probably want Vernon. He runs things around here.",
    ('pcbdded.msg', '242'): 'Okay.',
    ('pcbdded.msg', '268'): 'The mine could still be brought back. What is it you do here?',
    ('pcbdded.msg', '269'): "Yes, the mine's finished. Nothing left to do out there. What is it you do here?",
    ('pcbrtra.msg', '379'): "I've worked on this model before. There's a trick or two for getting more power out of the beam.",
    ('pcbrtra.msg', '381'): 'All right. A couple of parts will need replacing.',
    ('pccasadm.msg', '1337'): 'Ah, our new hire. What a relief to hand off some responsibility, even the small things.',
    ('pccasadm.msg', '212'): 'Bye now.',
    ('pccasbar.msg', '1212'): "Hey, look - it's the arena champion! Well, there's a surprise. Oh, hold on. I know it's not strictly by the rules, but I'd like to stand you a beer myself. Because that was something. (to himself) I'm going to be telling everyone about this...",
    ('pccltbhp.msg', '102'): '(1/3) You have the first statements in the case of the attacks.',
    ('pccltlzr.msg', '1101'): 'This vagrant drifts around the square with no particular purpose.',
    ('pccltlzr.msg', '1102'): 'This unhinged vagrant is loudly chanting something in honor of the church.',
    ('pccltlzr.msg', '1103'): 'This woman is so wasted she can barely cross the square.',
    ('pccltlzr.msg', '1104'): 'This refugee wanders the square with nowhere to go.',
    ('pccltptb.msg', '1213'): 'Excellent news! This day will go down in history as the day Phoenix was freed. You have my thanks, our gran guerrera.',
    ('pccltspy.msg', '1271'): "I'll give you a key and a Follower's robe. Tell the guards you're new, sent to deliver a report to the professor.",
    ('pccltspy.msg', '1319'): "You're trying my patience. Get out, you nuclear caterpillar!",
    ('pccltspy.msg', '1330'): "I'll admit it - I never expected a farm girl out of the wasteland to unravel this. I kept my work hidden even from Aaron. But you...",
    ('pccrvbos.msg', '1245'): 'Oh, certainly. As if the cultists would let a common farm girl into their chambers. Sure they would.',
    ('pccrvgrd.msg', '1101'): 'You see a caravan guard, getting ready for the road ahead.',
    ('pcctzn.msg', '400'): "They're saying Aaron is dead. Is it true?",
    ('pcdon.msg', '1301'): "I won't be barged in on and interrogated. Guards - throw this pushy senorita out of my casino.",
    ('pcdrgdlr.msg', '1205'): "Sure, sure, whatever you say, kid. But believe me, you're turning down the last bit of pleasure left in this lousy world.",
    ('pcmaster.msg', '1336'): "That's the killer! In the name of the Fire, stop her!",
    ('pcmaster.msg', '1344'): "I've heard enough for today. Thank you for talking with me.",
    ('pcmerkbs.msg', '1216'): '(raises an eyebrow) No. No trouble at all, greenhorn.',
    ('pcmerkbs.msg', '1260'): "Welco - hold on. Show me your neck. Those are collar marks, aren't they? It takes nerve for a runaway slave to walk in here. What do you want?",
    ('pcmerkbs.msg', '1266'): "Hm. The tinkers won't pay the same price for a runaway twice. You're putting me in an awkward position. Very well - I'll buy out your rights and sign your papers. But it will cost a thousand caps, and I doubt you're carrying that.",
    ('pcmerkbs.msg', '1270'): '(narrows her eyes, studying your face) Hm. Word came through recently about a certain highway bandit. And you fit the description a little too well.',
    ('pcmerkbs.msg', '1322'): "Hey - don't act like you set a criminal loose. It's the other way around!",
    ('pcmerkgd.msg', '1101'): "One of the guild's mercenaries. She's watching you closely.",
    ('pcpost.msg', '261'): 'Of course. Each locker costs ',
    ('pcpost.msg', '263'): "That's more than I can afford.",
    ('pcpost.msg', '264'): "Good. I'll take a locker.",
    ('pcpost.msg', '265'): 'Very good. You can use it any time.',
    ('pcpost.msg', '267'): 'I need another locker.',
    ('pcprtzne.msg', '1103'): 'Fear the Sacred Fire, scavenger.',
    ('pcprtzne.msg', '1202'): "Words worthy of a heretic and a blasphemer. Pray the Sacred Fire doesn't strike you down for that tongue of yours!",
    ('pcprtzne.msg', '1250'): 'An initiate? What are you doing here?',
    ('pcprtzne.msg', '1260'): "An initiate? Hm. I haven't seen you before. What are you doing here?",
    ('pcprtzne.msg', '1261'): "You're mistaken, fool. I'm no initiate. And that mistake is going to cost you your life!",
    ('pcprtzne.msg', '1263'): "An initiate? No, I don't even know what you're...",
    ('pcredbos.msg', '1329'): "You're lying. Boys - deal with this trash...",
    ('pcredpst.msg', '1256'): "That's right. You're one of those tough bitches the ring couldn't break. Respect. Show me a few moves sometime?",
    ('pcrngbos.msg', '1328'): 'Today Big Mario Albright finds out what losing feels like. Take me to the ring, Angelo. Take me out there as the next champion!',
    ('pcrngbos.msg', '1330'): "Not bad at all for a first timer, even if you took a beating. There's something there. You should keep at it.",
    ('pcrngbos.msg', '1331'): "Not bad at all for a first timer. You've got the makings. Worth building on.",
    ('pcrngbos.msg', '1363'): "Here's the thing. You're the champion now. Unbeaten. Follow me? We haven't got a fighter left to put in front of you, and I don't see one turning up soon. And if the crowd starts betting on you and winning, we make nothing. We earn on the bets that LOSE. Understand?",
    ('pctrener.msg', '1287'): "Come back when you're a saint radiating waves of goodness. Then I'll teach you everything I know.",
    ('pctrener.msg', '1332'): "(with contempt) I knew you couldn't be trusted. You swore an oath to use what I taught you for good. Now I don't believe a word out of your mouth. Leave me alone!",
    ('pipboy.msg', '10032'): ' they doubled my wages at the plant!',
    ('pipboy.msg', '10033'): " There's an upside to everything.",
    ('pipboy.msg', '10081'): ' that these allow aliens to adapt to a',
    ('pipboy.msg', '11064'): ' But we will not allow it. The library will be our',
    ('pipboy.msg', '11065'): ' fortress, knowledge our weapon, faith our shining armor.',
    ('pipboy.msg', '11066'): ' God help us.',
    ('pipboy.msg', '2062'): ' Our future is our land and our children.',
    ('pipboy.msg', '2063'): ' Protect them. Preserve our way. Avoid the',
    ('pipboy.msg', '2064'): ' technologies of the ancients. Drive outsiders away',
    ('pipboy.msg', '2065'): ' before they can cause harm. If one generation',
    ('pipboy.msg', '2066'): ' breaks the covenant, the community will fall.',
    ('pipboy.msg', '2067'): ' Just as Vault 27 once fell.',
    ('pipboy.msg', '7058'): ' and we are ready to support your undertakings.',
    ('pipboy.msg', '7060'): ' And remember - History is on your side.',
    ('pipboy.msg', '8199'): ' in the end, thanks to their greater numbers they did manage it',
    ('pipboy.msg', '9037'): ' Respectfully,',
    ('pipboy.msg', '9038'): ' Vault-Tec Public Relations Department',
    ('pipboy.msg', '9039'): ' Phoenix, Arizona',
    ('pvcovrsr.msg', '1305'): "You have my word as a Follower of the Sacred Fire - I'll be careful.",
    ('pvcovrsr.msg', '1356'): 'So how do I stay out of sight?',
    ('pvsbomb.msg', '116'): 'No need. The church has already fallen.',
    ('quests.msg', '108'): "Decipher the deputy sheriff's holodisk",
    ('quests.msg', '1204'): 'Survey the area within two sectors of San Felipe',
    ('quests.msg', '210'): 'Clear the mutants out of the vault',
    ('raiders1.msg', '100'): 'You approach a cave entrance in a mountainside.',
    ('raiders1.msg', '101'): 'You approach a ring of crumbling ruins. An old well sits in the center, with a ladder leading down into it.',
    ('raiders1.msg', '102'): "You've broken the raiders' back. They won't be operating in this region anymore.",
    ('raiders2.msg', '101'): "You're in a maze of caves. Pitch black. You can hear scorpions clicking.",
    ('raiders2.msg', '102'): 'These caves are being used as a barracks by a raider band.',
    ('rcacvcld.msg', '217'): "Well... honestly, I don't know. Shame Garth can't help us. He was tough. I saw him go down into the aqueduct himself once. Nothing scared him. He'd have kept us safe from anything!",
    ('rcacvcld.msg', '218'): 'What do you want for it?',
    ('rccomndr.msg', '396'): "Then I'm not letting this go. I'll take it all the way to the general himself!",
    ('rcrngqrz.msg', '273'): "It's dangerous here. Understand? VERY DANGEROUS! High radiation, and the people who live here have lost their minds. So off you go, if you value your life... Then again, warning you is all I'm obliged to do. Go on if you like. Just don't expect me to come save you.",
    ('rh_leonz.msg', '331'): "Thank you. You've been a real help.",
    ('rscmpsrv.msg', '265'): "The sect is collapsing and under persecution. City rebels destroyed the Followers' main base. Only scattered bands of cultists still pose any danger.",
    ('scboss.msg', '1282'): "Well. For all your antics, credit where it's due. I'd never have guessed one country girl could pull off something that complicated. So I'm willing to give you a chance to make it right.",
    ('sccmpbos.msg', '1234'): "Deserter! There's a tribunal waiting for you! Not one more step onto this base!",
    ('sccmpbos.msg', '1254'): 'Outstanding work, warrior!',
    ('scnisgvn.msg', '1562'): "I'm tired. Can it wait until I've rested?",
    ('scnisgvn.msg', '2146'): "I'm headed for the raider base at Ogima Black Cloud's asking. Is there anything you can tell me?",
    ('scnisgvn.msg', '2149'): "Can you make a strong poison? There's a drinking water tank at the raider base. If someone were to poison it...",
    ('scnisgvn.msg', '2178'): "The Sky Mother did not give me the healer's gift for that! I mend people, I don't destroy them. And in truth... I wouldn't know how to make a poison at all. If you're set on carrying that weight, your road runs straight to New Reno.",
    ('scnisgvn.msg', '2180'): 'They make poison there? Who, exactly?',
    ('scnisgvn.msg', '2181'): 'How do you know about Reno?',
    ('scnisgvn.msg', '2183'): "A city of devils, not far to the southwest. Better to stay away from it. Then again, there's nothing else that size anywhere near. I'll mark it on your map - but be careful there, and keep out of the back quarters.",
    ('scnisgvn.msg', '2184'): 'I don\'t remember names. I doubt they have any. Ask around the places men drink. In New Reno you hear "I want someone poisoned" more often than you hear hello.',
    ('scnisgvn.msg', '2185'): "No one of our tribe has walked so many roads or met so many people as I have. It's a long telling - the Cheyenne go back a great many years. There was much to see to, and our gods guided me... You see that irrigation cistern across from Ogima's hut? The wondrous technology of New Reno had a hand in that.",
    ('scnisgvn.msg', '2186'): 'I see. Well. Time I went to the raiders.',
    ('scnisgvn.msg', '471'): "Let's talk about something else.",
    ('scnisgvn.msg', '562'): "I'm tired. Can it wait until I've rested?",
    ('scnisgvn.msg', '694'): "That's it. I've had enough. I'm leaving.",
    ('scnisgvn.msg', '719'): "Don't forget anything. We need tools and medicine: ",
    ('scpatrla.msg', '120'): 'The patrolman spots you, but your disguise holds.',
    ('scpatrla.msg', '122'): "Hey, stop! Who's that? Ah, never mind...",
    ('scpatrla.msg', '124'): 'Rodge, is that you out there?',
    ('scpatrla.msg', '125'): 'Rodge, is that you? Out throwing up again?',
    ('scpatrul.msg', '1387'): 'A handful of Mexican anarchists. They refused to answer to anyone, so I killed their captain, and the rest sailed off wherever the wind took them.',
    ('scpatrul.msg', '370'): 'I travel a lot. I could scout the land for you.',
    ('scpatrul.msg', '371'): 'Yes, perhaps you could. When we arrived we surveyed the coastline and found no settlements at all. But word has reached us lately that someone has put down roots on the far side of the sea. Go there and find out everything about that settlement. And if there really are people living there, they will answer to us.',
    ('scpatrul.msg', '373'): "I'm here about the coastline survey.",
    ('scpatrul.msg', '374'): 'Well? What did you find? Is there a settlement out there?',
    ('scpatrul.msg', '375'): 'No, sir. Nothing so far.',
    ('scpatrul.msg', '376'): 'And if there really are people out there, what do you intend to do with them?',
    ('scpatrul.msg', '377'): "We'll give them a choice - answer to us, or move well clear of here. These are our lands now, and we won't have outsiders on our doorstep. Nothing unreasonable about it.",
    ('scpatrul.msg', '380'): 'There is a settlement on that shore. A small group of Mexicans came ashore there, running from their own government.',
    ('scpatrul.msg', '381'): 'Anarchists, then? Tell them the rules are different here. Either they answer to us willingly, or we make them.',
    ('scpatrul.msg', '382'): "They're peaceful people. I'll try to come to terms with them.",
    ('scpatrul.msg', '383'): "They've barely any weapons. I could just shoot the lot of them. I'll report when it's done.",
    ('scpatrul.msg', '384'): "Mexican refugees are living on that shore. They're willing to answer to you if you help them survive out there.",
    ('scpatrul.msg', '385'): "Hm. Not bad. We'll help them in exchange for seafood and a watch on those waters. Thank you for your service.",
    ('scpatrul.msg', '387'): 'A handful of Mexican anarchists. They refused to answer to anyone, so I killed their captain, and the rest sailed off wherever the wind took them.',
    ('scpatrul.msg', '388'): "The right call. Anarchists on our doorstep were the last thing we needed - who knows what they'd have got into their heads? Thank you for your service.",
    ('scpatrul.msg', '389'): "A handful of Mexican anarchists. But they'd already weighed anchor and gone wherever the wind took them.",
    ('scpatrul.msg', '390'): "Good riddance! Anarchists on our doorstep were the last thing we needed - who knows what they'd have got into their heads? Thank you for your service.",
    ('scscrbos.msg', '219'): 'Bye now.',
    ('scsldtlk.msg', '1210'): "Ah, our new hero! The upstart out of the desert who showed up every veteran we've got. Not bad. But don't imagine the Brotherhood takes you in that easily.",
    ('scsldtlk.msg', '1221'): "Hey, initiate. What'll it be - filling your worthless time with food, or hearing a veteran talk about the service?",
    ('scsldtlk.msg', '1255'): "Bit rich for an outsider off the wasteland, isn't it? Fine. But your stake goes up - fifty caps.",
    ('scsldtlk.msg', '216'): "I can't for the life of me work out how they let you aboard the ship, never mind gave you a title. What is the Brotherhood coming to...",
    ('scsldtlk.msg', '226'): 'Bye now.',
    ('scsldtlk.msg', '353'): 'His problem was a simple one, just not an obvious one.',
    ('sjohny.msg', '1553'): 'All right, tell me about the caravans again.',
    ('sscmpbos.msg', '247'): '"...The war with the super mutants goes on. Our brothers and sisters are giving their lives for the safety of California. More than that - the survival of our people depends on those sacrifices. That is why our mission in the Sonoran wasteland matters as much as it does..."',
    ('tcbndbos.msg', '1206'): "Then let's see what you have to say hanging over a burning barrel. Grab the spy, lads!",
    ('tcbndbos.msg', '1224'): "I'm just a mercenary. I don't much care who I work for.",
    ('tccrvqst.msg', '1264'): "Sort out your own problem. I've dealt with mine.",
    ('tccrvqst.msg', '205'): "As it happens, I'm carrying an energy cell like that.",
    ('tcctztlk.msg', '103'): 'Our conversation is of no consequence.',
    ('tccult.msg', '1230'): "As it happens, I'm a Follower of the Fire myself.",
    ('tcgate.msg', '1225'): "Good. I'd be glad of a fair deal.",
    ('tcgate.msg', '1238'): "See this robe? I'm a Follower of the Fire. We're on good terms with your people.",
    ('tcmedic.msg', '1251'): '(frowning) Master Hard has approved your treatment. But spending our most valuable implants on a savage out of the desert is beyond all reason!',
    ('tcmedic.msg', '1254'): "Master Hard thinks me worthy. I doubt he'd object to one operation.",
    ('tcmedic.msg', '236'): 'Just fix whatever you can.',
    ('tcmedic.msg', '270'): "I see. Then I'll try to get permission out of Hard.",
    ('tcmotel.msg', '1217'): 'As a Follower of the Fire, I am appalled by the service here!',
    ('tcpost.msg', '261'): 'Of course. Each locker costs ',
    ('tcpost.msg', '263'): "That's more than I can afford.",
    ('tcpost.msg', '264'): "Good. I'll take a locker.",
    ('tcpost.msg', '265'): 'Very good. You can use it any time.',
    ('tcpost.msg', '267'): 'I need another locker.',
    ('tshelmap.msg', '100'): "You've come upon someone's homestead, but nobody's around.",
    ('tshelpac.msg', '100'): 'You see Pacman.',
    ('tshelpac.msg', '101'): 'Welcome to our humble shelter.',
    ('tshelpac.msg', '102'): "You wouldn't happen to have a GECK, would you?",
    ('tshelpac.msg', '103'): 'Come back to us as soon as you can.',
    ('tshelpac.msg', '104'): 'You have a long road ahead.',
    ('tshelpac.msg', '105'): 'Look in our archive room.',
    ('tshelpac.msg', '106'): "Hurry. You don't have much time.",
    ('tshelpac.msg', '107'): 'We know more about you than you do (smiles).',
    ('tshelpac.msg', '200'): "The permanent leader of the project. This man deserves a special 'Enormous Thank You'. Thanks to him, over 60% of the game's text was translated!!! Afterward, almost all the text was checked and edited.",
    ('tshelsec.msg', '100'): 'You see a man with a scar.',
    ('tshelsec.msg', '101'): "This man seems vaguely familiar, but you can't place him. On his sleeve is a 'Red Scorpions' patch.",
    ('tshelsec.msg', '200'): "Put your weapon away if you don't want trouble.",
    ('tshelsec.msg', '201'): "You won't need a weapon. Nobody will hurt you here.",
    ('tshelsec.msg', '202'): "Don't do anything stupid and everything will be fine.",
    ('tshelsec.msg', '203'): "Don't make me angry. I've got a banhammer.",
    ('tshelsec.msg', '250'): 'You were warned.',
    ('tshelsec.msg', '300'): 'Go talk to somebody else.',
    ('tshelsec.msg', '301'): "Respect yourself and others, and you'll live.",
    ('tshelsec.msg', '302'): "We're good guys, for the most part.",
    ('tshelsec.msg', '303'): "I'm watching you. There's nothing to steal here.",
    ('tshelsec2.msg', '100'): 'You see a charismatic robobrain.',
    ('tshelsec2.msg', '101'): "This machine isn't off-putting and even looks rather amusing, but don't be fooled.",
    ('tshelsec2.msg', '200'): "Put your weapon away if you don't want trouble.",
    ('tshelsec2.msg', '201'): "You won't need a weapon. Nobody will hurt you here.",
    ('tshelsec2.msg', '202'): "Don't do anything stupid and everything will be fine.",
    ('tshelsec2.msg', '203'): 'A 14 gauge gun with automatic loading.',
    ('tshelsec2.msg', '250'): "Dead or alive, you're coming with me!",
    ('tshelsec2.msg', '300'): "I'd buy that for a dollar!",
    ('tshelsec2.msg', '301'): 'Serve the public trust, protect the innocent, uphold the law - are you sure about that?',
    ('tshelsec2.msg', '302'): 'Hey, you. Did you see that light too?',
    ('tshelsec2.msg', '303'): 'Subject placed under surveillance.',
    ('tshelter.msg', '101'): 'You see a shelter terminal.',
    ('tshelter.msg', '102'): "You can't read during combat.",
    ('tshelter.msg', '103'): "Your computer skills aren't sufficient.",
    ('tshelter.msg', '104'): 'Using this computer requires scientific knowledge.',
    ('tshelter.msg', '105'): 'Using this computer takes more than pressing a button.',
    ('tshelter.msg', '110'): 'Terminal 07.',
    ('tshelter.msg', '111'): 'Life support and climate control system.',
    ('tshelter.msg', '112'): 'Do nothing and observe.',
    ('tshelter.msg', '113'): "Project 'FRs'.",
    ('tshelter.msg', '114'): 'Personal diary [part 1].',
    ('tshelter.msg', '115'): 'Personal diary [part 2].',
    ('tsheltrl.msg', '100'): 'You see one of the translators.',
    ('tsheltrl.msg', '101'): 'Archives, archives, arch... [spits].',
    ('tsheltrl.msg', '102'): 'Ah! Good to see you.',
    ('tsheltrl.msg', '103'): '...What a moonlit night... (laughs).',
    ('tsheltrl.msg', '104'): 'Doing nonsense is the hardest thing of all.',
    ('tsheltrl.msg', '105'): "I'll gladly hear about your exploits once I've finished writing, thank you.",
    ('tsheltrl.msg', '106'): 'I agree with every false statement I have ever made.',
    ('tsheltrl.msg', '107'): 'Charge! [ahaha].',
    ('tsheltrl.msg', '200'): 'A person who took part in deciphering the archives (translating the text).',
    ('vcbabula.msg', '1305'): "You're a hypocrite hiding her own stupidity behind the outside world! Leave, and don't come back. I curse you, ",
    ('vcchrisb.msg', '1213'): 'I think I missed part of this story. Tell me the rest.',
    ('vcchrisb.msg', '253'): 'Goo-od! Me look for food!',
    ('vcchrisb.msg', '257'): 'Okay.',
    ('vccrzenm.msg', '1222'): 'The community will never forgive you for this! Everyone will know you let a traitor walk!',
    ('vccrzenm.msg', '235'): "Because it was a lie, idiot. The community is wrong. You don't execute your own people for being afraid.",
    ('vccrzenm.msg', '236'): "You're right, actually. I'm sorry, Chris, but the execution goes ahead as a lesson to the rest. To the square!",
    ('vcctzbld.msg', '1200'): 'All hail our savior!',
    ('vcjose.msg', '1246'): "Heaven be praised, you're back - and you brought the others with you! And I never even got to say a word to you before you left. Look at you!",
    ('vcjose.msg', '1251'): 'Amiga, go find something to keep yourself busy, would you?',
    ('vcjose.msg', '236'): 'Fanks.',
    ('vcjose.msg', '237'): 'Okay.',
    ('vcjose.msg', '244'): 'Ba-boom! Big bang-bang! Many peoples!',
    ('vcjose.msg', '246'): "Heaven be praised, you're back - and you brought the others with you! And I never even got to say a word to you before you left. Look at you!",
    ('vcjose.msg', '304'): "Don't worry! It'll all come right!",
    ('vcjose.msg', '305'): "I hope so. Let's get back to my questions.",
    ('vcjose.msg', '306'): 'I just wanted to say thank you for standing by me. It means a great deal, Uncle Jose.',
    ('vcjose.msg', '307'): "Hey, enough of that! I'm just a trader with a bad leg. The elders don't let me anywhere near their secrets.",
    ('vcjose.msg', '308'): "All right, let's talk about something else.",
    ('vckidpwr.msg', '1201'): "Greetings, child. From this day the Big Iron Maiden watches over you. Bad people won't dare come near.",
    ('vckidpwr.msg', '1202'): '(her eyes go wide with wonder, then she runs off to tell everyone about the Big Iron Protector)',
    ('vcmadre.msg', '284'): 'Maybe I can come to terms with the mine administration and get them to leave us alone?',
    ('vcmadre.msg', '285'): "The mine owner needs hands. He won't rest until his labor shortage is solved. I doubt there's a compromise to be had.",
    ('vcmadre.msg', '286'): "And what if it's time we changed? Ties with Garage City would put us ahead.",
    ('vcmadre.msg', '287'): "It's yours to decide which road we take now. But understand - a new way of living will come hard to our people.",
    ('vcmerarh.msg', '238'): "Err... I'm afraid I can't tell you that either. Not much, really...",
    ('vcmntad1.msg', '300'): 'David. Are we square?',
    ('vcmntad1.msg', '301'): 'I keep my word. Clear off.',
    ('vcmntad1.msg', '303'): 'All right. So what will you do now?',
    ('vcmntad1.msg', '304'): "I'm not staying in this town another day. I need to run - as fast and as far as I can!",
    ('vcmntptx.msg', '123'): "You... I know your kind! Cunning, so very cunning... Give me your hand - I need to see what color your blood runs! I won't survive another anal probing. [He pulls out a knife]",
    ('vcold.msg', '1284'): 'I must also share grievous news. Senor Andres, the padre of your savior, died in the years of slavery. (a cry goes up) By the rules of the community, his place of honor passes to his direct descendant. ',
    ('vcposola.msg', '1200'): "Greetings, gran heroe. So it's you we have to thank for an alliance this strong? You're the best of the best. But you can rest now and get back to your own affairs. We rangers will keep order in Villa and the country around it.",
    ('vcriper.msg', '274'): 'That mother of yours, the great pot-bellied hyena -',
    ('vcriper.msg', '275'): "I'd work her over and paint the room red,",
    ('vcriper.msg', '276'): 'our miserable kitchen, our nursery; her skull',
    ('vcriper.msg', '277'): "I'd set out for a chamber pot right by the bed.",
    ('vcriper.msg', '278'): 'And a shame that your father was carved by my hand',
    ('vcriper.msg', '279'): "into twenty-odd pieces - I'd love one more view! -",
    ('vcriper.msg', '280'): 'a year back, and hauled off in bits by the jackals.',
    ('vcriper.msg', '281'): "My Ripper's gone rusty. It's thirsty. It's due.",
    ('vcriper.msg', '282'): 'And your cousin as well, with that wife of his too -',
    ('vcriper.msg', '283'): "no, they're not a concern of mine now, not tonight.",
    ('vcriper.msg', '284'): 'Ah, the beautiful way that the pair came apart!',
    ('vcriper.msg', '285'): 'All praise to you, Nobel, and your fine dynamite!',
    ('vcriper.msg', '286'): 'Fewer kin left to you - and the fonder I grow.',
    ('vcriper.msg', '287'): 'Oh, I do love you, friend. Life is simple and sweet.',
    ('vcriper.msg', '288'): "Just remember, next time, if you'd save yourself trouble:",
    ('vcriper.msg', '289'): "make sure that she's orphaned before you two meet!",
    ('vcrobot.msg', '1203'): "Lo siento, mi joven descendiente. Technically I am a machine of the Old Times. But what matters far more is that I am the person of Felix Tejada, your direct ancestor. Don't be alarmed, great-great-granddaughter. There were robots like me all across this continent once.",
    ('vctibbet.msg', '300'): "Leon says he sold you his rifle. I'd like to buy it back.",
    ('vctibbet.msg', '301'): "I told him the tables would leave him with nothing, but he was sure he'd walk out rich. All kinds of fools come to Vegas and lose themselves here. I hope you're not one of them.",
    ('vctibbet.msg', '302'): "I'm not. What about the rifle?",
    ('vctibbet.msg', '303'): "I've got the rifle. I won't sell it cheap, though - I've grown fond of it myself [smiles]. Here's the deal: four thousand bucks and it's yours. Oiled, cleaned, ready to fire.",
    ('vctibbet.msg', '304'): 'Would you take three thousand?',
    ('vctibbet.msg', '305'): "Not a chance. That rifle's modified, one of a kind. No money, no deal - on your way.",
    ('vctibbet.msg', '306'): "Fine, agreed. I don't hunt anyway, and you'll get more use out of it.",
    ('vctibbet.msg', '307'): "Let's see the cash.",
    ('vctibbet.msg', '310'): "I'm broke right now. I'll come back.",
    ('vsstrbig.msg', '110'): "The stairway is blocked. There's no getting up it now.",
    ('vvcscnc.msg', '1467'): 'Greetings to my rescuer.',
    ('vvcscnc.msg', '387'): 'No need for that now. I found the diaries - it was all written down in them.',
    ('vvcscnc.msg', '469'): "What in hell happened here?! The cathedral destroyed?! That's the last thing I expected to find!",
    ('vvcscnc.msg', '492'): 'Okay.',
    ('vvcscnc.msg', '496'): 'Take armor off.',
    ('vvcscnc.msg', '501'): 'Oooh, ghosties! Not want to be ghostie!',
    ('vvsinrcm.msg', '199'): 'Villa and shelter have same ancestor. Me want to know!',
    ('wcprvtdi.msg', '152'): "You keep at it. I'll step away for a minute.",
    ('wcprvtdi.msg', '200'): '...Jim was no coward, and Jim was no hero,',
    ('wcprvtdi.msg', '201'): 'and the soldiering ground on the way that it goes.',
    ('wcprvtdi.msg', '202'): 'Jimmy put a round through the belly of heaven,',
    ('wcprvtdi.msg', '203'): 'and the wounded sky answered in rain, as it does.',
    ('wcprvtdi.msg', '204'): 'The weak are the first to go down in a war,',
    ('wcprvtdi.msg', '205'): "and an army's a wolf-path you walk till you fall.",
    ('wcprvtdi.msg', '206'): 'So Jimmy dies somewhere outside of Guangdong:',
    ('wcprvtdi.msg', '207'): "Jimmy's shot went wide - and the Red's didn't at all...",
    ('whrabbit.msg', '100'): 'You see a young Indian. Something about him sets him apart from the rest of his tribe.',
    ('whrabbit.msg', '101'): 'You see Slim White Rabbit, yawning and picking his nose.',
    ('whrabbit.msg', '102'): 'You see Slim White Rabbit. He looks very pleased to have come along with you.',
    ('whrabbit.msg', '103'): 'You see Slim White Rabbit, glancing around and taking in everything closely.',
    ('whrabbit.msg', '166'): 'All right, backing off.',
    ('whrabbit.msg', '167'): 'Give me a moment.',
    ('whrabbit.msg', '2002'): "Throwing stones. There's nothing else to do around here. What I want is to leave this village and go looking for something worth doing.",
    ('whrabbit.msg', '2004'): "The chief won't let me go. I promised Niskigwan I'd bring back his pack of herbs, and I couldn't. There are too many raiders - more than I can handle. I think I overestimated myself.",
    ('whrabbit.msg', '2007'): "Good. Then I'm coming with you.",
    ('whrabbit.msg', '203'): "So what's stopping you? I could use a hand on the road - want to come with me?",
    ('whrabbit.msg', '205'): "He's got the pack back. You're free to leave the tribe.",
    ('whrabbit.msg', '206'): "I might be able to get that pack back. Don't go far - I'll return soon.",
    ('whrabbit.msg', '208'): 'Keep up. The wastes are waiting.',
    ('whrabbit.msg', '300'): "You don't look much like the rest of your tribe.",
    ('whrabbit.msg', '301'): "My father was a caravan man out of Reno. He came through this tribe once, met my mother, fell in love and never left. She died bringing me into the world, so my father raised me - taught me to speak properly, told me about the wastes, all of it. The other children never let up. White Rabbit, they called me. I've always known I don't belong here.",
    ('whrabbit.msg', '303'): 'Tell me your story again.',
    ('whrabbit.msg', '5008'): 'Spears mostly, or a sledgehammer, or a knife. My father taught me to shoot a submachine gun too, but I never got good at it.',
    ('whrabbit.msg', '508'): 'What weapons do you use?',
    ('whrabbit.msg', '510'): 'Can you make healing powder?',
    ('whrabbit.msg', '512'): 'Remind me what healing powder takes?',
    ('whrabbit.msg', '515'): 'I can make healing powder from a broc flower and a xander root.',
    ('whrabbit.msg', '516'): "I'll need one broc flower and one xander root.",
    ('whrabbit.msg', '517'): "Let's see now... where to start... [You watch Slim make the healing powder.]",
    ('whrabbit.msg', '519'): "No trouble. But I'll need a spear.",
    ('whrabbit.msg', '521'): 'A little know-how, and there we are... [You watch Slim sharpen the spear.]',
    ('whrabbit.msg', '552'): "It's just a wound... a couple of stimpaks wouldn't hurt.",
    ('whrabbit.msg', '553'): 'I need a doctor. Now.',
    ('whrabbit.msg', '560'): "All right. I'll try to keep up.",
    ('whrabbit.msg', '561'): "No problem. I'll keep a middle distance.",
    ('whrabbit.msg', '562'): "Sure. I'll hang well back.",
    ('whrabbit.msg', '563'): 'I need you to stay close to me.',
    ('whrabbit.msg', '564'): "Don't get too far from me.",
    ('wscomprd.msg', '153'): 'Cell occupant: Sam Riley, of Las Vegas. Currently presumed dead.',
    ('wscomprd.msg', '154'): 'Cell occupant: Sam Riley, of Las Vegas. Currently at large.',
    ('xcprsdnt.msg', '1141'): 'Oh! Miss wants to know! But can we tell her, hm? Yes - now that all those silly people have left our apartments, we *can* tell Miss the truth.',
    ('xcprsdnt.msg', '141'): 'Oh! Mister wants to know! But can we tell him? Yes - now that all those silly people have left our apartments, we *can* tell Mister the truth.',
    ('ycbosgrd.msg', '115'): 'The boss has a lot on his plate. Hard to catch him in one place these days.',
    ('ycbossa.msg', '1283'): 'Give me a weapon, if you want me alive at the other end of the road to the Old Town.',
    ('ycbossa.msg', '1306'): "Senorita, I'm always glad to hear you out and answer your questions. ",
    ('ycbossb.msg', '1352'): "You can't get in there right now - the old military toys are still awake. Here are the access codes. They have to go out over that radio link you got working in San Isidro; we've no other transmitter strong enough. Once it's done, come to the pier and an escort will be waiting. And not a word of this to Gustavo!",
    ('yccafea.msg', '1302'): "Oh, you're saving us! Hey, everyone, look - this smoothskin just did us a real service. Thank her!",
    ('yccafea.msg', '1305'): "Oh, you're saving us, friend! Hey, everyone, thank her!",
    ('yccafeb.msg', '1232'): 'Pity. And I had my hopes up for a decent drink...',
    ('yccnvbos.msg', '1231'): "Well, you surprised me. Fine - bring me ten microchips. That'll be enough to make all this suffering worth something. After that we head north to trade.",
    ('yccnvbos.msg', '1245'): "Bah! I took you for another ghoul woman. You're just ugly. We've no use for your sort. Clear off.",
    ('yccrvmtn.msg', '1205'): "Kucha, friends with a normie? Ho-ho-ho, not a chance! She's your slave. Kucha, you surprise me. Set the slave aside and help us pull those normies out of that fortress.",
    ('yccrvmtn.msg', '1207'): 'That tongue of yours is too long, slave. Let me shorten it!',
    ('yccrvmtn.msg', '1209'): "Kucha, tell them I'm not a slave and that they need to leave those people alone.",
    ('ycdesant.msg', '1248'): "Ahh, ah! I love the smell of caps in the morning. Fine, kid. You've earned half, fair and square.",
    ('ycdesant.msg', '1273'): "There's one more job. It pays well - a full 500 hubbucks. But mind yourself, kid. I don't tolerate failure.",
    ('ycdesant.msg', '1356'): "That's damned bad news, and I don't care for bad news. You've disappointed me, kid. Go on. I've no more work for you.",
    ('ycdnvna.msg', '1102'): 'Thank you, amiga. Without you this would have ended very badly.',
    ('ycfungs.msg', '1200'): "Whoa there, sis! Don't kick off here, you're on my private property, more or less. Well... I don't mind you being here. Just keep it in mind.",
    ('ycghlmat.msg', '1200'): "Hey, senorita, what book are you out of? I don't recall reading about you.",
    ('ycghlmat.msg', '1240'): 'You beat ME? Extra-ordinary!',
    ('ycgopstp.msg', '1207'): 'Good girl... And well off too, by the look of you. Another ten caps.',
    ('ycgopstp.msg', '1228'): "Stop! I'm talking to you, you damned normie.",
    ('ychsptla.msg', '1103'): "What have we here? A ghoul's pet, or a free scavenger? Either way, you're not walking out of here...",
    ('ychsptlb.msg', '1208'): 'Never thought a normie would be the one to help me, and in the heart of the radioactive ruins at that. Thank you, friend.',
    ('ychsptlb.msg', '201'): 'Hey, friend, give me a hand! I got caught in a collapse - only a little one, but it broke a couple of bones. These old houses are past saving...',
    ('ycisdmtb.msg', '1216'): "Shut your mouth, scavenger! We're no filthy mutants - we are pure-blooded soldiers of the Creator!",
    ('ycliveb.msg', '1233'): "(sighs) Listen, friend. Do you really think I'd be hanging around here if I wanted Judy back?",
    ('ycmessag.msg', '1203'): '"Esteemed senorita, I know what you have done in the Sonoran desert. Whatever drives you and whatever you are working toward, experience like yours is beyond price."',
    ('ycnslbos.msg', '1219'): "Back then I was working the plantations and knew nothing about any war with super mutants. That's what I love about country life.",
    ('ycnslbos.msg', '1221'): 'Right. Now I need to find somewhere to clean myself up. Thank you, sister.',
    ('ycnslbos.msg', '226'): 'Safe travels. Try not to run into any more mutants.',
    ('ycnslmtn.msg', '1203'): 'Hey, I just watched him run off toward the piers! While you were talking to thin air, he was gone.',
    ('ycpirtlk.msg', '1200'): 'John told me about you. Said you were a clever little thing. Only how do you plan to storm an island with a pretty smooth face like that?',
    ('ycpirtlk.msg', '1203'): "John told me about you. Said you were a clever little thing. I hope you understand what's waiting for you on that island.",
    ('ycpirtlk.msg', '1227'): "You've got one job, smoothskin - shut down the combat readiness system so the robots and the guns stop firing at everything that moves. We'll work out what to haul off the island ourselves.",
    ('ycralf.msg', '1210'): "Thank you, Ralph. I'd be very grateful.",
    ('yctalius.msg', '1396'): "Right. As if I'd believe that. Sure, sure. Goodbye, Talius, you charlatan.",
    ('yctalius.msg', '278'): "You know, I used to be an atheist. But once fate made you immortal, it's hard not to start believing in a plan. Maybe this is a trial of some sort.",
    ('ysend.msg', '102'): 'Before setting out you dropped some things you no longer have any use for (',
    ('ysgaubi.msg', '116'): 'You strip some parts out of the howitzer.',
    ('ytinfo.msg', '150'): 'Further north the road disappears into the sand.',
    ('ytinfo.msg', '151'): 'This is the road you came in on from Sonora. To go back, wait for departure at the assembly point.',
    ('ytinfo.msg', '152'): 'Collapsed buildings block the road.',
    ('ytinfo.msg', '153'): "The bridge is down. With a little ingenuity, that won't stop you climbing to the bottom.",
    ('zccrvgrd.msg', '121'): "Nobody left to pay us, so we're done here.",
    ('zccrvgrd.msg', '122'): 'Split the goods and go our separate ways.',
    ('zcdsprdo.msg', '100'): 'You see a bandit.',
    ('zcdsprdo.msg', '101'): 'You see a Mexican who has gone thoroughly to the bad. They call scoundrels like him desperados.',
    ('zcfloatr.msg', '110'): 'That looks like the last of them.',
    ('zcfloatr.msg', '111'): 'One of the monsters got away from the fire.',
    ('zcplgrm.msg', '1150'): "Sorry, my rotting amiga, but you can't come with us.",
    ('zcplgrm.msg', '1151'): "Never thought I'd run into somebody out here as ugly as me.",
    ('zcplgrm.msg', '1153'): 'The normies run you off too? We know that one well.',
    ('zcplgrm.msg', '1154'): "We'd take you along, but we don't know where we're going ourselves.",
    ('ziposta.msg', '110'): "The storage locker has a solid lock on it. You'll have to talk to the administrator.",
    ('zsgrvgen.msg', '130'): 'Do we really have to do this?',
    ('zsgrvgen.msg', '131'): "I've done my share of grave robbing. You know how it is.",
    ('zsgrvgen.msg', '132'): "I doubt there's anything worth having in there.",
    ('zsgrvgen.msg', '141'): 'You think this is all right?',
    ('zsgrvgen.msg', '142'): "The rangers wouldn't like this one bit.",
    ('zsgrvgen.msg', '150'): "You think there's anything valuable down there?",
    ('zsgrvgen.msg', '151'): 'Makes no difference to me. Just make sure nobody sees us.',
    ('zsgrvgen.msg', '152'): 'The Mexicans would never forgive us for this.',
    ('zsgrvgen.msg', '160'): 'God! Have you got no conscience at all?',
    ('zsgrvgen.msg', '161'): "Don't tell me this is in the name of science.",
    ('zsgrvgen.msg', '170'): 'Bah! How did I ever end up with you?',
    ('zsgrvgen.msg', '171'): 'Robbing graves? The order takes a dim view of that.',
    ('zsgrvgen.msg', '180'): "I'm going to pretend I didn't see that.",
    ('zsgrvgen.msg', '190'): "Quite right. They've no use for it, and we do.",
    ('zsgrvgen.msg', '192'): "Don't sweat it. No judgment here. I've done the same.",
    ('zslump.msg', '115'): 'The fire drives the floating monsters back.',
}
